## Worked example 1 -- the standard launcher (do this when you can)

A 1v1 story duel, via PoD's own entry point. The minigame intercepts it if
the gates pass and vanilla resolves it if they don't. Note
`INVALIDATION_EVENT`, which the raw builder has no equivalent for: it fires
if attacker and defender turn out to be the same character.

```
configure_start_single_combat_effect = {
    SC_INITIATOR       = scope:actor
    SC_ATTACKER        = scope:actor
    SC_DEFENDER        = scope:recipient
    FATALITY           = no
    FIXED              = no
    LOCALE             = terrain_scope
    OUTPUT_EVENT       = my_namespace.0001
    INVALIDATION_EVENT = my_namespace.0002
}
```

---

## Worked example 2 -- minimal 1v1 through the builder

The simplest possible builder call, for reference. In production, prefer
example 1: this route loses your saved scopes.

```
scope:actor = {
    POD_combat_create_duel_effect = {
        INITIATOR    = scope:actor
        ATTACKER     = scope:actor
        DEFENDER     = scope:recipient
        FATALITY     = possible
        FIXED        = no
        LOCALE       = terrain_scope
        OUTPUT_EVENT = my_namespace.0001
    }
    POD_combat_duel_add_enemy_effect = { CHARACTER = scope:recipient }
    POD_combat_finalize_duel_effect  = yes
}
```

